---
/**
 * SignalCard — the card under the instrument (2026-09-30, the export round): the work room's card, for SIGNAL. Always
 * open (Jon, 2026-10-07: the same law as the case studies). The "?" key in the instrument's head lands on its TOP
 * ([data-write-up]): the title and the words in view, the diagram beneath them. 96 px under the device: air, still SIGNAL's (a room gap would detach it). Inside: the
 * write-up (signal-card-copy.ts, Jon's to rewrite) · HOW TO PLAY (./HowToPlay.astro: one keyboard diagram drawn from
 * signal-copy.ts LEGEND, 2026-10-06) · UNDER THE HOOD (the engine, a spine of steps) · WHERE IT CAME FROM. Mounted by StudioOne's play room (inside .sig-desktop, so
 * it exists only where the instrument plays) and by /signal.
 * 2026-10-13 (ONE ANATOMY): the card is a `.sheet` (src/styles/sheet.css), the material, rhythm and parts the
 * work-room sheets share: the kind word over its title (round two: the numbered readout line is gone), a hairline and
 * a label opening each section, the steps' spine. That file is its only dependency outside this folder; what stays
 * here is its own: the title, the 96 px under the device, the sapphire, and the names HowToPlay reads.
 * 2026-10-13 round four (Jon: "I want the white sheet to go underneath the signal instrument to make it feel like
 * it's one thing"): `part="around"` is the homepage's play room: ONE sheet that carries the kind word, the title and
 * the story, then the device (the host's slot: its own stage, scaled and fitted from StudioOne), then how to play,
 * under the hood and where it came from. The paper runs on behind the device; powered, the device is wider than the
 * sheet and overhangs both its edges (the host keeps every box overflow-visible). Inside it the sheet's own rhythm:
 * story → device 56, device → how to play's hairline 56 (the host's stage margins). The "?" key's landing,
 * [data-write-up], is the HOW TO PLAY section there (its hairline and label in view at the top); on "all" (the
 * default: the whole card, 96 px beneath the device, as /signal mounts it) it is still the whole card.
 * (Round three's "head" / "tail" halves, two sheets around the device, are retired with it.)
 * THE CUT (2026-10-22, Jon: "Claude built that, and that's stupid that I would say that ['Your first song is in your
 * downloads'] before they even touched the instrument"): the card at rest is the kind word, the title, (the device),
 * HOW TO PLAY and ONE line under it, the dare. The story, under the hood and where it came from leave (their strings
 * stay commented in signal-card-copy.ts). THE RECEIPT comes back the moment it is true: the instrument emits no event,
 * but its export cap takes `.saved` in the same tick it hands the WAV to the browser (export-view.ts `land()`); the
 * card watches the export corner for that class and prints the receipt IN THE DARE'S SLOT (one grid cell, so nothing
 * moves), in the card's accent, for the rest of the visit. The instrument itself is untouched.
 * THE FEELING (2026-10-22, late; Jon: "not the safety. it's the feeling of having made something, easily, instantly,
 * tangibly"): the dare leaves; the slot is THREE MOVES (his content, DRAFT) and moves ABOVE how to play, right under
 * the device; the receipt in it is his line, "Good or bad, you just made a demo."
 */
import "../../styles/sheet.css";
import { CARD } from "./signal-card-copy.ts";
import HowToPlay from "./HowToPlay.astro";

interface Props { part?: "all" | "around" }
const { part = "all" } = Astro.props;
const around = part === "around";

---

<div class="sc sheet" data-signal-card data-part={part} data-write-up={around ? undefined : ""}>
  <p class="sheet-kind">{CARD.kind}</p>
  <h4 class="sc-title">{CARD.title}</h4>

  {around && <slot />}

  {/* THE MOVES (2026-10-22, late): one slot under the device. At rest the three moves; once a song is printed, the
      receipt in its place (the script below fills it, so a screen reader hears it then) */}
  <div class="sc-line">
    <p class="sc-moves">{CARD.moves.map((m, i) => <span>{i > 0 && " "}{m}</span>)}</p>
    <p class="sc-receipt" role="status" data-line={CARD.receipt}></p>
  </div>

  <div class="sheet-sec sc-how" data-write-up={around ? "" : undefined}>
    <p class="sheet-t" id="how-to-play">{CARD.howTitle}</p>
    <HowToPlay />
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  // THE RECEIPT (2026-10-22): the export cap ([data-ctl="export"] in the [data-corner="export"] corner) takes `.saved`
  // the moment the WAV is handed to the browser; until then the receipt would be a lie. Watch the corner (static in
  // Signal.astro; the cap mounts into it once the take is ready), print once, stop watching.
  const corner = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-corner="export"]');
  const card = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-signal-card]");
  const line = card?.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".sc-receipt");
  if (corner && card && line) {
    const mo = new MutationObserver(() => {
      if (!corner.querySelector('[data-ctl="export"].saved')) return;
      mo.disconnect();
      line.textContent = line.dataset.line ?? "";
      card.setAttribute("data-printed", "");
    });
    mo.observe(corner, { subtree: true, childList: true, attributes: true, attributeFilter: ["class"] });
  }
</script>

<style>
  /* the card's own; the sheet (material, inks, night, the kind word, sections, steps) is src/styles/sheet.css */
  .sc {
    --sheet-acc: #4fd1ff; /* the instrument's own light: the keys' sapphire */
    /* HowToPlay's diagram reads these two names; they follow the sheet's ink (day and night) and mono */
    --sc-ink: var(--sheet-ink);
    --sc-mono: var(--sheet-mono);
    position: relative;
    margin: 0 auto; /* "around": the host's room spaces it like the other sheets */
    padding: var(--sheet-pad); /* the bottom: the last section's 16 + the gutter = the work sheets' 16 + their handle */
  }
  /* the "?" key's landing: the whole card from its top (/signal), or how to play's hairline + label (the homepage) */
  [data-write-up] { scroll-margin-top: 32px; }
  .sc[data-part="all"] { margin-top: 96px; } /* the whole card, 96 px under the device (/signal) */
  /* the band-name's face, to the letter (Jon, 2026-10-15: SIGNAL read as a different font next to the other titles;
     it was 2.125rem with 0.06em tracking): Outfit 500 3.25rem/1.05, −0.02em; 2.5rem under 900 */
  .sc-title {
    margin: 0 0 40px;
    text-align: center;
    font-family: var(--sheet-display);
    font-size: 3.25rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  @media (max-width: 899px) {
    .sc-title { font-size: 2.5rem; }
  }
  /* THE CUT (2026-10-22): the title → the device is the device stage's own 56 (StudioOne), as band → object on the
     work sheets; on /signal the title → how to play's hairline keeps the 40 */
  .sc[data-part="around"] .sc-title { margin-bottom: 0; }
  /* THE LINE: the moves and the receipt in ONE grid cell (one slot, so nothing below moves), in the display face at
     the house floor line's size (1rem/1.6, centered, 62ch). Since THE FEELING (2026-10-22, late) it stands under the
     device: the stage's own 56 above it (StudioOne; on /signal the title's 40), 32 to how to play's hairline */
  .sc-line {
    display: grid;
    margin: 0 auto 32px;
    max-width: 62ch;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .sc-line > p {
    grid-area: 1 / 1;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--sheet-display);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    text-wrap: balance;
    transition: opacity 0.4s ease;
  }
  .sc-moves { color: var(--sheet-ink); }
  /* a narrow sheet: a line each */
  @container sheet (max-width: 619px) {
    .sc-moves > span { display: block; }
  }
  /* the receipt: the card's sapphire mixed toward the ink until 4.5:1 on the paper by day (the hints' recipe), bare
     at night, where the sapphire is already light on dark */
  .sc-receipt {
    --rc-mix: 56%;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sheet-acc) var(--rc-mix), var(--sheet-ink));
    opacity: 0;
  }
  :global(html[data-night]) .sc-receipt { --rc-mix: 100%; }
  .sc[data-printed] .sc-moves { opacity: 0; }
  .sc[data-printed] .sc-receipt { opacity: 1; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .sc-line > p { transition: none; }
  }
</style>
